WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.110
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.380 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.390 --> 01:37.770
[Episode 12]

4
01:39.800 --> 01:42.590
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

5
01:41.200 --> 01:41.560
Come.

6
01:41.870 --> 01:43.000
Come, Comrade Li De.

7
01:43.070 --> 01:44.400
Easy.

8
01:46.870 --> 01:48.039
Comrade Li De.

9
01:47.950 --> 01:50.310
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

10
01:48.710 --> 01:49.759
Bo Gu.

11
01:52.039 --> 01:52.590
Listen.

12
01:52.800 --> 01:55.180
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

13
01:54.350 --> 01:55.560
You must not waver.

14
01:55.560 --> 01:56.560
You know me.

15
01:56.880 --> 01:58.120
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission; Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

16
01:57.729 --> 01:58.590
You understand me.

17
01:58.120 --> 01:59.410
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

18
02:00.430 --> 02:01.680
Comrade Li De.

19
02:04.060 --> 02:05.060
I understand you.

20
02:06.150 --> 02:07.040
I understand.

21
02:07.180 --> 02:08.699
I'll help him back to rest first.

22
02:08.699 --> 02:09.210
Okay.

23
02:09.360 --> 02:10.160
Let's go back.

24
02:12.870 --> 02:13.670
What's wrong?

25
02:14.110 --> 02:16.579
I firmly oppose all of Mao's opinions.

26
02:16.900 --> 02:21.180
Enough. Let's go back. Let's go.

27
02:18.280 --> 02:19.590
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission (CRMC); Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army]

28
02:21.050 --> 02:22.720
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

29
02:34.550 --> 02:36.150
Let's continue the meeting.

30
02:39.120 --> 02:41.520
Judging from the current enemy situation,

31
02:41.560 --> 02:43.680
entering Guizhou first may be

32
02:44.240 --> 02:47.150
our best chance of meeting less resistance.

33
02:48.310 --> 02:50.160
But our strategic route north to western Hunan

34
02:50.160 --> 02:51.940
to link up with the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

35
02:51.940 --> 02:54.660
must not change.

36
03:01.590 --> 03:03.320
Then let's proceed as follows.

37
03:04.970 --> 03:08.190
In the name of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

38
03:08.190 --> 03:09.630
we'll order all army corps to break free of the enemy quickly

39
03:09.630 --> 03:10.710
and move west into Guizhou

40
03:10.710 --> 03:11.720
to maneuver for

41
03:11.970 --> 03:13.570
a subsequent advance north.

42
03:13.620 --> 03:15.030
If during this process,

43
03:15.430 --> 03:17.079
the enemy situation changes significantly,

44
03:17.079 --> 03:18.870
we will hold a meeting in due course

45
03:18.870 --> 03:20.310
to discuss new decisions.

46
03:20.310 --> 03:21.680
What do you think?

47
03:24.660 --> 03:26.180
Seek truth from facts.

48
03:27.450 --> 03:28.380
All right.

49
03:36.579 --> 03:37.740
I agree.

50
03:43.960 --> 03:46.000
The military situation is urgent and brooks no delay.

51
03:46.000 --> 03:47.240
I'll go to the Military Commission to draft a telegram right away.

52
03:47.240 --> 03:48.079
I'll go with you.

53
03:48.079 --> 03:48.560
Okay.

54
03:48.800 --> 03:51.000
Comrades, that concludes the meeting.

55
03:51.840 --> 03:54.570
Be sure to mark the telegram as extremely urgent.

56
03:58.410 --> 04:00.480
The meeting is over. Let's go.

57
04:03.800 --> 04:06.730
We didn't get to the bottom of things in that meeting.

58
04:07.790 --> 04:10.720
We clearly had the majority,

59
04:11.000 --> 04:12.180
yet look at the outcome.

60
04:12.180 --> 04:13.560
They rejected

61
04:13.580 --> 04:15.910
the most important part of your proposal.

62
04:15.930 --> 04:17.260
We can't go on like this.

63
04:17.810 --> 04:18.940
If we have a meeting,

64
04:18.980 --> 04:21.420
we must hold a formal Politburo meeting.

65
04:21.839 --> 04:22.660
The current situation where the Troika

66
04:22.660 --> 04:24.710
overrides the Politburo

67
04:25.420 --> 04:27.130
must be changed.

68
04:28.580 --> 04:30.440
We still gained something today.

69
04:30.720 --> 04:31.980
Although Bo Gu and Li De

70
04:32.510 --> 04:34.920
still insist on heading north to western Hunan,

71
04:34.920 --> 04:38.480
they have agreed to move west into Guizhou first,

72
04:38.800 --> 04:40.190
then head north.

73
04:40.620 --> 04:43.540
A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.

74
04:43.540 --> 04:45.690
Taking the first step is crucial.

75
04:46.060 --> 04:48.300
More importantly, Comrade Enlai

76
04:48.540 --> 04:49.890
has a clear attitude.

77
04:50.370 --> 04:51.570
With his support,

78
04:52.250 --> 04:54.310
many things will be easier to handle.

79
04:54.940 --> 04:56.620
Comrade Zeng Xisheng

80
04:56.940 --> 04:58.010
and Comrade Qian Zhuangfei

81
04:58.010 --> 05:00.660
are our eyes and ears.

82
05:00.980 --> 05:02.520
Their intelligence report just now

83
05:02.520 --> 05:03.890
came right on time.

84
05:04.010 --> 05:05.940
This is clearly Comrade Enlai's work.

85
05:05.940 --> 05:08.370
Comrade Enlai is meticulous in his work.

86
05:08.620 --> 05:09.880
It's truly admirable.

87
05:10.010 --> 05:12.250
This meeting was indeed fruitful.

88
05:12.620 --> 05:14.150
Just as Comrade Enlai said,

89
05:14.270 --> 05:15.670
your cold stove

90
05:16.060 --> 05:17.980
is finally heating up.

91
05:19.330 --> 05:21.540
You finally have an important voice

92
05:22.060 --> 05:25.320
and the right to make suggestions at the military meeting.

93
05:26.830 --> 05:28.290
It's been quite a journey.

94
05:29.540 --> 05:31.940
Come, let me carry you back.

95
05:32.740 --> 05:33.659
Oh, spare me.

96
05:33.810 --> 05:34.980
I was gritting my teeth in pain

97
05:34.980 --> 05:36.860
the whole way here.

98
05:37.180 --> 05:38.510
My stove's finally hot.

99
05:38.570 --> 05:40.450
Maybe the heat

100
05:40.450 --> 05:41.980
will disinfect your wound.

101
05:42.250 --> 05:43.620
Kill some germs.

102
05:45.900 --> 05:51.110
[Outside Tongdao County Town, Hunan]

103
06:04.690 --> 06:05.620
Bo Gu.

104
06:06.370 --> 06:08.250
Our compromise has its limits.

105
06:08.250 --> 06:10.250
Our compromise has its limits.

106
06:10.250 --> 06:12.210
After arriving in Guizhou,

107
06:12.210 --> 06:16.010
we must deploy to head north as soon as possible.

108
06:16.450 --> 06:17.510
Comrade Jiaxiang.

109
06:18.010 --> 06:18.810
Thank you.

110
06:19.010 --> 06:20.470
Thank you, Comrade Enlai.

111
06:21.300 --> 06:23.620
Send an immediate telegram to the 2nd and 6th Corps.

112
06:23.620 --> 06:26.300
Order them to advance at once into the upper Yuan River region

113
06:26.300 --> 06:28.560
to tie down enemy forces in western Hunan

114
06:28.940 --> 06:31.400
and cover the Central Red Army's movements.

115
06:31.540 --> 06:32.620
To tie down enemy forces in western Hunan

116
06:32.620 --> 06:35.080
and cover the Central Red Army's movements.

117
06:40.659 --> 06:44.100
Look, Comrade Zedong has really recovered.

118
06:44.300 --> 06:45.690
He's riding a horse.

119
06:47.010 --> 06:48.210
Comrade Zedong.

120
06:48.300 --> 06:49.980
If I remember correctly,

121
06:50.210 --> 06:52.010
this is the first time you've ridden a horse

122
06:52.010 --> 06:53.740
since the strategic transfer.

123
06:54.890 --> 06:56.420
Tongdao is a good place.

124
06:56.810 --> 06:59.620
Tongdao, the road to heaven.

125
06:59.860 --> 07:01.320
I've been lying down for so many days.

126
07:01.320 --> 07:02.980
It's time to spur the horse on.

127
07:03.890 --> 07:04.500
Bo Gu.

128
07:05.740 --> 07:07.690
Mao has recovered.

129
07:08.230 --> 07:10.230
His spirit is much better than mine.

130
07:15.450 --> 07:16.620
Comrade Zedong.

131
07:16.980 --> 07:18.130
Your momentum

132
07:18.300 --> 07:21.330
reminds me of Du Fu's famous poem.

133
07:22.370 --> 07:24.980
The Ferghana horse is famous among barbarian steeds.

134
07:24.980 --> 07:27.330
Its lean frame is sharply defined.

135
07:27.620 --> 07:29.860
Its ears stand tall like split bamboo.

136
07:30.060 --> 07:32.320
And its four hooves are light in the wind.

137
07:32.330 --> 07:34.659
No terrain can bar its way.

138
07:34.860 --> 07:37.810
It's a steed you can trust with your life.

139
07:38.060 --> 07:39.659
Such a steed, so swift and bold.

140
07:39.659 --> 07:41.940
Could gallop ten thousand miles, free and untold.

141
07:41.940 --> 07:43.100
I have a poem too.

142
07:43.770 --> 07:45.450
The desert sand is like snow.

143
07:45.810 --> 07:47.860
The moon over Mount Yan is like a hook.

144
07:47.860 --> 07:49.720
When will I wear my golden bridle;

145
07:49.740 --> 07:52.300
and gallop through the crisp autumn night?

146
08:04.560 --> 08:07.230
What are they babbling about?

147
08:07.540 --> 08:09.270
They are talking about horses.

148
08:09.450 --> 08:10.710
Talking about horses?

149
08:12.980 --> 08:14.210
When I recover,

150
08:14.810 --> 08:16.660
I will also get a good horse.

151
08:17.730 --> 08:19.370
Wait until you recover.

152
08:21.250 --> 08:23.890
On December 12, 1934,

153
08:24.210 --> 08:27.080
an emergency meeting of the CPC Central Committee leadership decided

154
08:27.080 --> 08:29.350
to move west into Guizhou to seek room

155
08:29.370 --> 08:30.980
to maneuver before advancing north.

156
08:30.060 --> 08:35.309
[Liping, Guizhou]

157
08:31.060 --> 08:33.860
This became known as the Tongdao Strategic Shift.

158
08:34.260 --> 08:35.659
On December 15,

159
08:35.909 --> 08:36.900
the 1st Red Army Corps

160
08:36.900 --> 08:39.809
defeated the garrison of Guizhou warlord Wang Jialie

161
08:39.450 --> 08:41.659
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

162
08:40.020 --> 08:41.299
and captured Liping.

163
08:50.940 --> 08:51.810
Mao Zhenhua!

164
08:53.180 --> 08:54.510
Do you have a death wish?

165
08:57.260 --> 08:58.210
Don't worry, Commander.

166
08:58.010 --> 09:00.220
[Geng Biao, Commander of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

167
08:58.210 --> 09:00.010
I checked. There are no bullets.

168
09:00.850 --> 09:02.850
The firing pin can also hurt people.

169
09:03.210 --> 09:05.420
Even if it hurts people, it won't hurt our Red Army.

170
09:05.420 --> 09:07.350
It can only hurt the White bandits.

171
09:09.650 --> 09:10.410
Commander.

172
09:11.370 --> 09:12.410
I must say, this battle

173
09:12.410 --> 09:14.080
was fought with no spirit at all.

174
09:14.080 --> 09:15.110
What?

175
09:15.490 --> 09:17.940
Did a battle wear you out?

176
09:18.690 --> 09:20.300
It's not that it wore me out.

177
09:20.540 --> 09:22.660
It's just that it was completely boring.

178
09:22.660 --> 09:23.910
The pre-battle mobilization

179
09:23.910 --> 09:24.940
was so inspiring.

180
09:25.450 --> 09:27.250
For the attack on Liping County,

181
09:27.260 --> 09:28.920
they said there was a regiment

182
09:29.140 --> 09:31.200
of the Guizhou Army stationed there.

183
09:31.420 --> 09:32.540
I thought, wow,

184
09:32.730 --> 09:33.850
a whole regiment.

185
09:35.020 --> 09:36.120
Then I, Mao Zhenhua,

186
09:36.120 --> 09:37.580
must fight a bloody battle

187
09:37.810 --> 09:39.270
to do our commander proud.

188
09:39.640 --> 09:40.930
But when we charged in,

189
09:41.450 --> 09:43.610
I didn't even see a single person of the Guizhou Army.

190
09:43.610 --> 09:44.610
They all ran away.

191
09:44.780 --> 09:45.780
The locals said

192
09:46.060 --> 09:47.520
when the Guizhou Army ran,

193
09:47.610 --> 09:49.470
they threw away all their rifles,

194
09:49.610 --> 09:52.210
but didn't drop a single opium pipe.

195
09:52.660 --> 09:53.490
I figured,

196
09:53.520 --> 09:55.000
since we didn't catch any prisoners,

197
09:55.000 --> 09:57.260
it'd be good to capture some guns, right?

198
09:57.330 --> 09:59.060
We can't go back empty-handed.

199
09:59.210 --> 10:00.270
But what happened?

200
10:01.090 --> 10:02.540
Look, Commander.

201
10:03.850 --> 10:06.050
This gun doesn't even have rifling.

202
10:06.940 --> 10:07.730
I heard

203
10:07.850 --> 10:10.960
this is an imitation from Wang Jialie's Chishui Arsenal,

204
10:10.960 --> 10:13.290
commonly known as the "Nine-Shot Stick".

205
10:14.100 --> 10:15.500
You kid,

206
10:16.270 --> 10:19.060
you won a battle and still have so many complaints.

207
10:19.060 --> 10:20.090
Let me ask you,

208
10:20.260 --> 10:23.330
would you rather fight the Hunan Army, the Guangxi Army,

209
10:23.330 --> 10:25.210
or the Guizhou Army?

210
10:25.810 --> 10:27.020
If you ask me that,

211
10:27.050 --> 10:29.310
I'd still rather fight the Guizhou Army.

212
10:29.610 --> 10:31.610
If the enemies at the Xiang River were that easy to fight,

213
10:31.610 --> 10:34.420
our regiment wouldn't have lost so many soldiers.

214
10:36.060 --> 10:37.180
That's why

215
10:37.610 --> 10:39.060
the strategic shift at Tongdao was so crucial.

216
10:39.060 --> 10:40.320
Instead of heading to western Hunan,

217
10:40.320 --> 10:41.490
we turned toward Guizhou.

218
10:41.490 --> 10:42.380
Chengwu.

219
10:42.520 --> 10:43.780
Political Commissar.

220
10:43.860 --> 10:44.990
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

221
10:44.060 --> 10:44.810
Come,

222
10:46.980 --> 10:48.110
let me help you down.

223
10:48.830 --> 10:49.540
I'm fine.

224
10:49.660 --> 10:50.410
Are your injuries fully healed?

225
10:50.410 --> 10:51.130
Almost.

226
10:51.490 --> 10:52.810
I couldn't wait any longer,

227
10:52.810 --> 10:54.340
and I can't delay the march.

228
10:55.060 --> 10:56.320
Political Commissar.

229
10:56.780 --> 10:58.440
Your leg healed that quickly?

230
11:00.440 --> 11:02.440
Let me walk a few steps for you to see.

231
11:15.610 --> 11:16.450
How is it?

232
11:17.610 --> 11:20.180
That's why you're the Political Commissar.

233
11:20.450 --> 11:23.730
Even your leg has higher awareness than ordinary comrades.

234
11:23.730 --> 11:25.060
It heals just like that.

235
11:25.690 --> 11:27.730
Mao Zhenhua, what a mouth you have.

236
11:29.120 --> 11:31.120
Let's go, we'll talk while walking.

237
11:31.910 --> 11:34.840
Mao Zhenhua, continue cleaning up the battlefield.

238
11:37.170 --> 11:38.140
Come, let me help you.

239
11:38.140 --> 11:38.780
I'm fine.

240
11:42.350 --> 11:43.680
Making a strategic shift

241
11:43.680 --> 11:44.520
at Tongdao

242
11:45.870 --> 11:46.730
was a good move.

243
11:47.680 --> 11:54.160
[Outside Changde, Hunan]

244
11:51.900 --> 11:52.540
Xiao.

245
11:54.300 --> 11:55.540
This Luo Qijiang

246
11:55.660 --> 11:57.090
is really overconfident.

247
11:57.090 --> 11:58.850
With just the 34th Independent Brigade

248
11:58.850 --> 11:59.980
garrisoning alone,

249
12:00.130 --> 12:02.300
he actually deployed his three regiments separately.

250
12:01.310 --> 12:06.470
[He Long, Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

251
12:02.810 --> 12:03.900
The distance between regiments

252
12:03.900 --> 12:05.450
must be dozens of miles.

253
12:05.710 --> 12:06.650
This is a good thing.

254
12:06.650 --> 12:07.560
A great thing.

255
12:07.850 --> 12:10.650
We can pick them off one by one and wipe them all out.

256
12:13.820 --> 12:14.610
Reporting!

257
12:14.700 --> 12:18.830
An urgent telegram from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

258
12:19.760 --> 12:21.360
[Xiao Ke, Captain of the 6th Red Army Corps]

259
12:23.180 --> 12:24.900
The Central Committee ordered us to go south

260
12:24.900 --> 12:26.570
to approach the upper reaches of the Yuan River

261
12:26.570 --> 12:28.090
and cover their north.

262
12:28.580 --> 12:31.140
They still want to continue north at this time?

263
12:31.140 --> 12:33.420
Western Hunan is a death trap right now.

264
12:33.970 --> 12:34.810
What a pity.

265
12:35.090 --> 12:36.570
We've deployed for so long,

266
12:36.570 --> 12:38.300
and all our efforts are wasted.

267
12:39.730 --> 12:41.210
The Central Committee ordered us to go south

268
12:41.210 --> 12:42.940
just to cover their march north

269
12:42.940 --> 12:45.000
to relieve their military pressure.

270
12:45.260 --> 12:46.190
Here's the plan.

271
12:46.240 --> 12:47.770
We'll attack Changde first

272
12:48.380 --> 12:49.640
to threaten Changsha.

273
12:49.780 --> 12:51.420
We'll use the strategy of besieging Wei to rescue Zhao.

274
12:51.420 --> 12:52.680
I don't believe He Jian

275
12:52.810 --> 12:54.020
would just stand by

276
12:54.180 --> 12:55.450
and let us attack Changsha.

277
12:55.450 --> 12:57.140
He will definitely withdraw troops to reinforce.

278
12:57.140 --> 12:59.140
Wouldn't that also ease

279
12:59.310 --> 13:02.090
the military pressure on the CPC Central Committee?

280
13:02.090 --> 13:03.020
So you're saying we should

281
13:03.020 --> 13:05.350
continue our offensive in western Hunan?

282
13:06.730 --> 13:08.090
The 34th Independent Brigade

283
13:08.090 --> 13:09.660
is well-equipped

284
13:10.020 --> 13:11.420
and ripe for the taking.

285
13:11.490 --> 13:13.290
Let's wipe them out completely.

286
13:13.420 --> 13:15.570
I'm just afraid the Military Commission won't agree

287
13:15.570 --> 13:16.970
and will hold us accountable later.

288
13:16.970 --> 13:19.260
Xiao, you always think too much.

289
13:19.450 --> 13:20.910
As long as it helps our cause,

290
13:20.910 --> 13:21.800
it doesn't matter how we fight

291
13:21.800 --> 13:23.140
or what form the battle takes,

292
13:23.140 --> 13:24.380
as long as we win.

293
13:24.610 --> 13:25.690
By then,

294
13:25.850 --> 13:28.140
if we draw more of He Jian's Hunan Army over,

295
13:28.140 --> 13:30.270
what can the Military Commission say?

296
13:30.330 --> 13:31.610
The most important thing now

297
13:31.610 --> 13:33.020
is to send a telegram to Comrade Bishi.

298
13:33.020 --> 13:34.220
If he also agrees,

299
13:34.780 --> 13:36.060
we'll do it immediately.

300
13:36.060 --> 13:36.650
Okay.

301
13:41.160 --> 13:41.920
Zhang.

302
13:42.540 --> 13:45.660
The right front hoof on your horse doesn't sound right.

303
13:45.850 --> 13:46.940
It needs a new horseshoe.

304
13:46.940 --> 13:49.180
Otherwise, it could stumble and throw you.

305
13:49.180 --> 13:50.380
It's very dangerous.

306
13:56.120 --> 13:58.450
It really is. Thank you, Corps Commander.

307
14:00.830 --> 14:05.800
[Mountainous Region, Guizhou]

308
14:01.070 --> 14:04.220
The Red Army is strong.

309
14:04.880 --> 14:08.840
♪ No hardship can hold us back ♪

310
14:09.210 --> 14:12.850
♪ On the march, we'll give Chiang a beating ♪

311
14:13.370 --> 14:16.850
♪ March north to fight the Japanese invaders ♪

312
14:17.810 --> 14:21.690
♪ The Red Army is strong ♪

313
14:22.090 --> 14:26.060
♪ No hardship can hold us back ♪

314
14:26.380 --> 14:29.690
♪ On the march, we'll give Chiang a beating ♪

315
14:29.690 --> 14:32.210
They finally sing again.

316
14:32.700 --> 14:33.770
Yes.

317
14:34.050 --> 14:37.060
Although Guizhou is mountainous and the roads are rough,

318
14:37.060 --> 14:39.330
the enemy isn't hot on our heels anymore,

319
14:39.680 --> 14:42.300
and we haven't seen any more Kuomintang's planes.

320
14:42.300 --> 14:44.430
Everyone's feeling a lot more at ease.

321
14:44.610 --> 14:46.260
The vanguard of the 1st Red Army Corps

322
14:46.260 --> 14:47.780
has been capturing towns

323
14:47.890 --> 14:49.940
and strongholds with barely a fight.

324
14:49.940 --> 14:52.180
The Guizhou Army flees at the mere sight of us.

325
14:52.180 --> 14:54.610
And our morale is greatly boosted.

326
14:55.230 --> 14:56.070
This proves

327
14:56.100 --> 14:56.980
Comrade Zedong

328
14:57.000 --> 14:59.210
was right all along about

329
14:59.560 --> 15:01.960
the Guizhou Army's poor fighting ability.

330
15:02.730 --> 15:04.690
♪ Everyone's up early ♪

331
15:05.060 --> 15:07.780
♪ Leading the cattle out to graze ♪

332
15:08.140 --> 15:10.140
♪ We search for tender grass to feed the cattle well ♪

333
15:10.610 --> 15:12.940
♪ So they can have their fill ♪

334
15:14.730 --> 15:16.010
The characters are correct.

335
15:16.010 --> 15:17.520
And the handwriting is neat.

336
15:17.520 --> 15:18.690
What about yours?

337
15:21.570 --> 15:23.170
The characters are correct,

338
15:23.700 --> 15:25.560
but what does "up for grass" mean?

339
15:25.850 --> 15:26.810
Up early.

340
15:27.330 --> 15:28.790
What is "tender morning"?

341
15:29.210 --> 15:30.880
It's tender grass. Chairman, I wrote it wrong.

342
15:30.880 --> 15:32.140
Rewrite it five times.

343
15:32.260 --> 15:33.060
Yes.

344
15:39.260 --> 15:40.170
What about Changbao's?

345
15:40.170 --> 15:42.470
I think I lost mine, Chairman.

346
15:42.490 --> 15:44.500
It rained heavily yesterday,

347
15:44.520 --> 15:47.280
and I was in a hurry to find the tarpaulin,

348
15:47.300 --> 15:48.790
so I accidentally

349
15:48.810 --> 15:51.090
lost the notebook.

350
15:51.780 --> 15:53.810
Squad Leader, you didn't lose it in the rain.

351
15:53.810 --> 15:54.970
When we set off this morning,

352
15:54.970 --> 15:55.780
you left it in the house.

353
15:55.780 --> 15:56.780
I kept it for you.

354
15:58.360 --> 15:59.190
Is it my notebook?

355
15:59.190 --> 16:00.550
It has your name on it.

356
16:11.210 --> 16:12.570
There are only about 20 characters in total.

357
16:12.570 --> 16:14.030
You got half of them wrong.

358
16:14.080 --> 16:16.900
Rewrite it ten times, and write one more character.

359
16:16.900 --> 16:17.900
Give me your hand.

360
16:24.830 --> 16:27.230
The character "qi" in "qipian" (deceive).

361
16:28.300 --> 16:29.830
"Q" often refers to others.

362
16:30.060 --> 16:31.690
"I" is deceiving.

363
16:32.230 --> 16:34.200
So deceiving others is ultimately deceiving oneself.

364
16:34.200 --> 16:36.680
Over time, you lose your sincerity.

365
16:37.060 --> 16:38.540
And you lose your courage.

366
16:38.780 --> 16:39.300
Without courage,

367
16:39.300 --> 16:41.520
how can you be a qualified Red Army soldier?

368
16:41.520 --> 16:43.120
How can you march to victory?

369
16:43.690 --> 16:44.210
Okay.

370
16:45.510 --> 16:46.630
I understand, Chairman.

371
16:46.630 --> 16:48.120
Write this character 20 times.

372
16:48.120 --> 16:48.760
Yes.

373
16:49.360 --> 16:50.890
Don't be afraid, grandson.

374
16:51.020 --> 16:52.400
There are too many people here.

375
16:52.400 --> 16:53.660
Let's walk on the side.

376
16:54.540 --> 16:55.340
That's right.

377
16:56.850 --> 16:58.260
Wait a little longer.

378
16:58.480 --> 17:00.740
I'll find you something good to eat soon.

379
17:02.180 --> 17:03.780
Yes, let's walk on the side.

380
17:03.810 --> 17:04.599
Old lady.

381
17:04.900 --> 17:05.730
Come, old lady.

382
17:05.730 --> 17:06.690
Let us help you to the side.

383
17:06.690 --> 17:07.780
It's crowded, and we don't want you getting bumped.

384
17:07.780 --> 17:08.440
Don't move.

385
17:08.770 --> 17:09.730
Let us help you to the side.

386
17:09.730 --> 17:11.290
I'm not blocking your way.

387
17:11.290 --> 17:11.859
We don't want you getting bumped.

388
17:11.859 --> 17:12.730
Don't make things difficult for me.

389
17:12.730 --> 17:13.380
Get up.

390
17:13.380 --> 17:14.660
I'm just a poor person.

391
17:15.099 --> 17:16.250
Please get up. We don't want you getting bumped.

392
17:16.250 --> 17:16.900
We'll walk on the side.

393
17:16.900 --> 17:18.339
Old lady, old lady.

394
17:18.339 --> 17:19.380
Get up quickly. Don't kowtow.

395
17:19.380 --> 17:21.510
Officers, we're not blocking the way.

396
17:21.819 --> 17:23.690
Officers, please spare our lives.

397
17:23.690 --> 17:25.380
You're not blocking the way, old lady.

398
17:25.380 --> 17:26.730
We are not officers.

399
17:27.180 --> 17:28.450
We are the Red Army.

400
17:28.970 --> 17:29.820
Red Army.

401
17:30.220 --> 17:31.690
Red Army?

402
17:32.690 --> 17:33.660
Old lady.

403
17:34.420 --> 17:36.210
Where are you coming from?

404
17:36.380 --> 17:37.710
And where are you going?

405
17:38.050 --> 17:41.530
I don't know where I'm going either.

406
17:41.940 --> 17:45.100
I just want to find a way for my grandson to survive.

407
17:46.660 --> 17:48.660
My son was conscripted.

408
17:48.840 --> 17:50.970
And my daughter-in-law died long ago.

409
17:51.280 --> 17:56.210
My grandson hasn't been able to walk since he was born.

410
17:56.870 --> 17:58.630
But I have hands.

411
17:58.650 --> 18:02.250
I'll use them to earn a living and support my grandson.

412
18:06.450 --> 18:07.560
Officers.

413
18:08.090 --> 18:09.220
Old lady.

414
18:09.820 --> 18:10.660
Get up.

415
18:11.680 --> 18:12.410
Don't kneel.

416
18:13.530 --> 18:14.050
Come.

417
18:32.220 --> 18:34.700
No, no.

418
18:34.850 --> 18:36.440
Officer, you can't.

419
18:47.260 --> 18:49.980
Old lady, let me sit with you for a while.

420
18:50.810 --> 18:52.090
We poor people

421
18:52.120 --> 18:54.840
are born with bad luck.

422
18:59.580 --> 19:01.530
Changfeng, get some food.

423
19:02.240 --> 19:03.280
Get a bit more.

424
19:11.020 --> 19:12.210
Old lady.

425
19:14.430 --> 19:17.300
You are good people.

426
19:17.700 --> 19:19.020
Good people.

427
19:22.160 --> 19:24.270
Grandson, we have food now.

428
19:24.290 --> 19:25.620
Look.

429
19:27.430 --> 19:29.260
Thank you, my benefactors.

430
19:31.610 --> 19:32.570
Grandson.

431
19:32.590 --> 19:34.260
We have food now.

432
19:44.630 --> 19:46.670
Look.

433
19:46.820 --> 19:48.670
I will give you one to taste.

434
19:49.240 --> 19:49.890
Here.

435
19:50.150 --> 19:51.150
Take it.

436
19:53.890 --> 19:55.370
Benefactors,

437
19:56.450 --> 19:58.050
where are you going?

438
19:58.340 --> 19:59.490
Old lady.

439
19:59.540 --> 20:01.680
We are going to find a way out

440
20:02.810 --> 20:04.810
for all the poor people in the world.

441
20:05.180 --> 20:06.050
Good.

442
20:06.400 --> 20:06.920
Good.

443
20:13.100 --> 20:14.030
Comrade Zedong.

444
20:14.380 --> 20:15.280
We can no longer be led by the nose

445
20:15.280 --> 20:17.110
by Li De's wrong commands.

446
20:17.620 --> 20:19.420
To solve the unresolved issues,

447
20:19.490 --> 20:20.490
we must hold a

448
20:20.660 --> 20:22.190
formal Politburo meeting.

449
20:22.200 --> 20:24.250
Yes, we must.

450
20:24.970 --> 20:26.570
Let's discuss it with Enlai.

451
20:30.820 --> 20:36.380
[Wang Jialie's Residence, Guiyang, Guizhou]

452
20:36.580 --> 20:38.050
Didn't the Communist army go to western Hunan?

453
20:38.050 --> 20:39.610
Why are they suddenly heading for Guizhou?

454
20:39.610 --> 20:42.450
[Wang Jialie, Commander of the Kuomintang's 25th Army and Chairman of Guizhou Provincial Government]

455
20:39.860 --> 20:43.210
You're asking me something even the Generalissimo hasn't figured out.

456
20:43.210 --> 20:45.250
The Communist army is advancing in force.

457
20:43.380 --> 20:45.650
[Wan Shufen, wife of Wang Jialie]

458
20:45.280 --> 20:47.870
With the limited troops of our 25th Army,

459
20:49.100 --> 20:50.340
we can't stop them.

460
20:50.380 --> 20:52.240
If we can't stop them, then don't.

461
20:53.360 --> 20:54.960
Let's follow Chen Jitang's example

462
20:54.960 --> 20:56.690
in Guangdong and let them pass.

463
20:57.210 --> 20:58.250
Smoke less.

464
20:58.460 --> 21:01.100
My fear is that the Communists aren't just passing through.

465
21:01.100 --> 21:04.210
If they settle in Guizhou,

466
21:04.490 --> 21:07.140
they'll turn our Guizhou into another Jiangxi.

467
21:07.140 --> 21:08.270
That we can't allow.

468
21:08.420 --> 21:10.010
If they turn Guizhou into another Jiangxi,

469
21:10.010 --> 21:11.290
we'll be finished.

470
21:11.450 --> 21:12.580
We must ask for help.

471
21:12.620 --> 21:13.510
Ask for help?

472
21:15.690 --> 21:18.010
I have already sent telegrams to all provinces.

473
21:18.010 --> 21:19.340
But so far,

474
21:19.860 --> 21:21.260
we've barely heard a word

475
21:21.450 --> 21:22.850
from the Sichuan, Hunan,

476
21:23.210 --> 21:24.740
Yunnan, or Guangxi armies.

477
21:26.230 --> 21:29.030
You still have the mood to smoke at a time like this?

478
21:32.430 --> 21:35.720
Who appointed you as the Chairman of Guizhou Province?

479
21:35.740 --> 21:36.980
What do you mean?

480
21:37.820 --> 21:39.050
You mean...

481
21:43.170 --> 21:44.370
ask Nanjing for help?

482
21:44.580 --> 21:46.210
Which of those armies,

483
21:46.250 --> 21:47.450
Yunnan, Hunan, Guangxi, or Sichuan,

484
21:47.450 --> 21:49.250
doesn't have its eye on your Guizhou?

485
21:49.250 --> 21:50.970
And you really trust that so-called mutual assistance pact

486
21:50.970 --> 21:52.170
you signed with them?

487
21:52.620 --> 21:54.620
Even if we invite them to reinforce us,

488
21:54.620 --> 21:57.290
they should be uniformly dispatched by Generalissimo.

489
21:57.290 --> 21:59.860
If they have ulterior motives,

490
22:00.530 --> 22:02.990
at least Nanjing can see justice done for us.

491
22:03.050 --> 22:04.450
What you say makes sense.

492
22:05.770 --> 22:08.630
I will send a telegram to Generalissimo right away.

493
22:08.940 --> 22:11.290
I will also send a telegram

494
22:11.450 --> 22:12.970
to Madame Chiang in my personal name,

495
22:12.970 --> 22:14.610
asking her to put in a good word for us

496
22:14.610 --> 22:16.340
in front of the Generalissimo.

497
22:17.450 --> 22:22.740
[Fenghua, Zhejiang]

498
22:20.620 --> 22:22.660
We are already home.

499
22:23.450 --> 22:25.770
I didn't see you eat much of

500
22:26.020 --> 22:28.500
the yellow croaker soup with greens earlier.

501
22:28.500 --> 22:30.260
The fish was the same,

502
22:30.660 --> 22:32.450
and so were the greens.

503
22:34.810 --> 22:36.700
But I'll probably never taste

504
22:37.820 --> 22:39.930
my mother's cooking again.

505
22:39.090 --> 22:42.120
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs of the Commission of Kuomintang]

506
22:43.190 --> 22:45.320
After all the exhausting travel,

507
22:45.860 --> 22:49.190
at least we made it in time for my mother's memorial service.

508
22:49.350 --> 22:50.840
Your filial piety

509
22:51.220 --> 22:53.460
is truly a model for the nation.

510
22:54.010 --> 22:55.380
Fighting everywhere

511
22:55.380 --> 22:56.960
and rushing about all these years,

512
22:56.960 --> 22:59.370
[Inner Residence]

513
22:57.450 --> 22:59.180
only this home is the one place

514
22:59.490 --> 23:02.730
[Song Meiling, Chiang Kai-shek's wife]

515
23:00.660 --> 23:03.530
where my heart can find peace.

516
23:04.790 --> 23:06.450
You've been too tired lately.

517
23:06.840 --> 23:09.990
Take this opportunity to rest for a few days.

518
23:28.050 --> 23:30.380
What's wrong? Everyone looks so worried.

519
23:31.210 --> 23:33.540
Is it because of the situation in Guizhou?

520
23:37.660 --> 23:39.730
The Communist army suddenly turning to Guizhou

521
23:39.730 --> 23:41.210
is indeed unexpected.

522
23:41.580 --> 23:44.140
The several defense lines we set up in western Hunan

523
23:44.140 --> 23:46.180
are probably going to be completely ineffective.

524
23:46.180 --> 23:47.580
What I'm most worried about now is that

525
23:47.580 --> 23:48.910
Wang Jialie's 25th Army

526
23:49.150 --> 23:51.170
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

527
23:49.420 --> 23:51.690
won't be able to stop the Zhu-Mao Communist army at all.

528
23:51.690 --> 23:53.540
They are constantly

529
23:53.690 --> 23:55.150
fleeing west step by step.

530
23:55.730 --> 23:57.490
They suddenly became agile.

531
23:58.120 --> 24:00.120
I think you should have noticed it.

532
24:01.400 --> 24:02.310
Yes.

533
24:02.620 --> 24:03.970
We have actually been paying close attention

534
24:03.970 --> 24:05.730
to the movements of the Zhu-Mao Communist army.

535
24:05.730 --> 24:06.770
This move

536
24:07.050 --> 24:08.250
really surprised me.

537
24:08.530 --> 24:09.970
But please rest assured, Generalissimo.

538
24:09.970 --> 24:11.090
Once there are new movements,

539
24:11.090 --> 24:12.950
I will report to you immediately.

540
24:13.580 --> 24:15.290
The Zhu-Mao Communist army entering Guizhou

541
24:15.290 --> 24:17.640
[Yang Yongtai, Secretary of Nanchang Headquarters]

542
24:15.380 --> 24:17.450
is not an absolutely bad thing.

543
24:17.820 --> 24:19.140
If they continue

544
24:19.340 --> 24:21.900
north to western Hunan along the eastern Guizhou route,

545
24:21.900 --> 24:24.010
we will still follow the previous plan:

546
24:24.010 --> 24:26.860
crush Zhu and Mao first, then take Hunan.

547
24:27.450 --> 24:30.140
What if they stay in Guizhou and don't leave?

548
24:30.490 --> 24:31.830
Then we will take the opportunity

549
24:31.830 --> 24:33.230
to secure Guizhou first,

550
24:33.380 --> 24:35.160
then move against Hunan and Guangxi.

551
24:35.160 --> 24:36.580
You are wise, Generalissimo.

552
24:36.580 --> 24:38.140
The only thing we must watch out for is

553
24:38.140 --> 24:39.170
making sure Hunan and Guangxi

554
24:39.170 --> 24:42.060
don't snatch up Guizhou first.

555
24:42.730 --> 24:43.420
Well said.

556
24:43.680 --> 24:45.140
Zurong, draft a telegram.

557
24:45.160 --> 24:45.720
Yes.

558
24:46.770 --> 24:48.660
Send an urgent order to Wang Jialie's forces

559
24:48.660 --> 24:50.690
to fall back to the Shibing-Taigong line

560
24:50.690 --> 24:52.730
and continue containing the Communist army.

561
24:52.730 --> 24:55.860
Hunan Army is to defend only along the eastern Guizhou line,

562
24:55.860 --> 24:58.510
while Guangxi Army must hold

563
24:58.550 --> 25:00.150
the Guizhou-Guangxi border

564
25:00.340 --> 25:02.340
and is not allowed to enter Guizhou.

565
25:02.420 --> 25:04.250
Also, order the two columns

566
25:04.530 --> 25:05.930
of Xue Yue's Central Army

567
25:06.180 --> 25:08.490
to advance immediately toward

568
25:08.660 --> 25:10.660
the Tongren-Yuping-Tianzhu line.

569
25:10.730 --> 25:11.290
Yes.

570
25:18.050 --> 25:20.180
Generalissimo, everything is ready at Ci'an.

571
25:20.180 --> 25:21.010
You can offer incense now.

572
25:21.010 --> 25:21.660
Good.

573
25:27.340 --> 25:36.490
[Liping County, Guizhou]

574
25:28.900 --> 25:31.660
On December 18, 1934,

575
25:32.010 --> 25:36.050
the CPC Central Committee held a Politburo meeting in Liping.

576
25:37.010 --> 25:38.730
There is only one topic today,

577
25:39.770 --> 25:41.490
which is to discuss the next direction of action

578
25:41.490 --> 25:43.730
for our Central Red Army.

579
25:43.060 --> 25:44.800
[Kaifeng (He Kefan), Alternate Member of the CPC Politburo and CPC Representative to the 9th Red Army Corps]

580
25:44.010 --> 25:46.360
Why didn't Comrade Li De attend the meeting?

581
25:46.360 --> 25:48.490
Comrade Li De had a malaria attack.

582
25:48.660 --> 25:50.070
His fever hasn't gone down yet,

583
25:50.070 --> 25:51.710
so he is absent from today's meeting.

584
25:51.710 --> 25:52.970
But he has entrusted me

585
25:52.970 --> 25:54.370
to express his opinions.

586
25:54.620 --> 25:57.770
Then please speak first, Comrade Bo Gu.

587
26:01.280 --> 26:03.810
I don't think it's necessary for us to discuss

588
26:03.820 --> 26:06.180
our next direction of action.

589
26:06.530 --> 26:08.210
Because our direction of action

590
26:08.210 --> 26:09.610
was decided beforehand.

591
26:10.010 --> 26:11.730
That is to go north to western Hunan,

592
26:11.730 --> 26:13.490
and join forces with the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps,

593
26:13.490 --> 26:15.990
and open up a new revolutionary base.

594
26:17.950 --> 26:18.910
Comrade Bo Gu,

595
26:19.380 --> 26:20.490
when we were in Tongdao,

596
26:20.490 --> 26:21.680
you didn't oppose

597
26:21.790 --> 26:23.770
[Liu Shaoqi, Alternate Member of the CPC Politburo and CPC Representative to the 8th Red Army Corps]

598
26:21.870 --> 26:24.010
the decision of the Central Red Army to enter Guizhou.

599
26:24.010 --> 26:25.870
Why are you going back on it today?

600
26:26.140 --> 26:28.540
Comrade Jiaxiang, I am not going back on it.

601
26:29.420 --> 26:31.530
Our decision to enter Guizhou was only

602
26:31.530 --> 26:33.770
a temporary maneuver to

603
26:34.050 --> 26:36.970
evade the Kuomintang pursuit.

604
26:37.180 --> 26:39.140
But we still haven't broken

605
26:39.620 --> 26:41.150
out of their encirclement.

606
26:41.490 --> 26:42.890
They have set up new traps

607
26:43.100 --> 26:44.380
in northeastern Guizhou

608
26:44.380 --> 26:45.770
and northwestern Hunan, waiting for us

609
26:45.770 --> 26:47.090
to fall into them.

610
26:54.940 --> 26:55.970
Comrade Bo Gu,

611
26:56.180 --> 26:57.340
I want to ask you.

612
26:57.660 --> 27:00.320
Since the beginning of the strategic transfer,

613
27:00.490 --> 27:03.100
we have lost contact with the Comintern

614
27:03.450 --> 27:04.620
for two months.

615
27:05.100 --> 27:07.710
Does the Comintern know

616
27:08.050 --> 27:12.180
what we've been through during these two months of strategic relocation?

617
27:12.820 --> 27:15.680
Does it know the deployment of the Kuomintang army?

618
27:15.810 --> 27:18.290
You're still relying on outdated information

619
27:18.290 --> 27:19.520
to judge today's situation.

620
27:19.520 --> 27:20.760
That won't work.

621
27:21.250 --> 27:22.050
We've only

622
27:22.170 --> 27:24.770
lost contact with the Comintern temporarily.

623
27:24.970 --> 27:25.940
That alone

624
27:26.000 --> 27:28.120
doesn't justify changing

625
27:28.160 --> 27:30.180
our established strategic direction.

626
27:30.180 --> 27:32.410
This is a matter of organizational discipline

627
27:32.410 --> 27:33.940
and political principles.

628
27:34.010 --> 27:36.180
Nothing is more important than finding a way

629
27:36.180 --> 27:38.380
for the Chinese Revolution to survive.

630
27:39.290 --> 27:40.290
A strategic direction

631
27:40.290 --> 27:42.050
isn't a cure-all.

632
27:42.290 --> 27:44.100
We must base our decisions on the realities on the ground.

633
